{
  "basic principles (trl 1): the report states the scientific or engineering principles on which the assessed technology is based, citing observations, studies or literature.": 1,
  "concept formulated (trl 2): the report describes a practical application of those principles and how the assessed technology is intended to work in it.": 2,
  "proof of concept (trl 3): the report presents analytical or laboratory results that demonstrate the critical function or characteristic of the assessed technology.": 3,
  "laboratory validation (trl 4): the report states that the assessed component or a low-fidelity breadboard was tested in a laboratory environment and reports the results.": 4,
  "relevant-environment validation (trl 5): the report states that the assessed component or breadboard was tested in a simulated or relevant environment representative of the intended environment, and reports the results.": 5,
  "prototype in relevant environment (trl 6): the report states that a representative model or prototype of the assessed system or subsystem was demonstrated in a relevant environment.": 6,
  "prototype in operational environment (trl 7): the report states that a prototype close to the final configuration was demonstrated in the actual operational environment.": 7,
  "system qualified (trl 8): the report states that the final system was completed and qualified through test and demonstration against its requirements.": 8,
  "proven in operation (trl 9): the report states that the final system was used successfully in actual operations or deployment over a stated period.": 9,
  "quantified results against requirements: the report compares measured performance with stated requirements or acceptance criteria and says whether they were met.": "performance",
  "environment and test article defined: the report describes the test conditions and the configuration or fidelity of the tested article (for example breadboard, prototype, production unit) relative to the intended application.": "conditions",
  "evidence matches the assessment target: the cited evidence concerns the assessed target itself (component, subsystem, system or technology), not a different element or only the parent project as a whole.": "scope"
}
